                        "glosses": [
                            "In an apheliotropic way; away from the sun."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8dd7d964-c017-477f-8883-c76c89b3dc1c",
                                "sense_id": "4fc64dc9-ea48-38cd-bdf9-a19c21f3bf22",
                                "text": "In the case of the radicles of Sinapis alba, sensitiveness to light also resides in the tip, which, when laterally illuminated, causes the adjoining part of the root to bend apheliotropically."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c7a44581-4d18-4f69-ae99-3f5023b590db",
                                "sense_id": "4fc64dc9-ea48-38cd-bdf9-a19c21f3bf22",
                                "text": "It has been empirically found that the reflection ratio when apheliotropically (looking downsun) is ..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ada0460a-91bb-44e6-909f-f0fecbfb445a",
                                "sense_id": "4fc64dc9-ea48-38cd-bdf9-a19c21f3bf22",
                                "text": "Where the red moon, inches above our heads, Will exclude us from its light, apheliotropically, in the end."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
